comments[9]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-04T13:15:31.270Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: all-status searches for tag push/changelog/release date/immutable tag found pm-lwnifd, pm-5baq, pm-db8onn, pm-2f80fn, pm-e70zh5, and pm-7zs0. Those own exact-tag recovery, generated alignment, recovery run selection, diagnostics, aggregate reliability, and release-health respectively; none owns ordinary tag-push changelog stabilization. Clean-room evidence: pnpm changelog:pm at immutable v2026.9.4 changes only CHANGELOG.md heading from '## 2026.9.4' to '## 2026.9.4 - 2026-09-04' plus transient managed-extension updated_at."
  "2026-09-04T13:17:35.982Z","harness:codex","TDD red evidence: focused release automation contract failed exactly because an ordinary tag push with RECOVERY_SOURCE_MODE=tag invoked pnpm changelog:pm:check instead of guarded regeneration. The workflow-presence assertion passed, isolating the defect to source-mode branching."
  "2026-09-04T13:39:57.878Z","harness:codex","Implementation and verification evidence: source-mode branching now treats every exact-tag source identically, keeps reviewed-main drift checks intact, and guards regeneration so only CHANGELOG.md may change. Focused workflow contracts pass; full coverage passes 603 files and 8,356 tests at exact 100/100/100/100; quality:static, typecheck, docs links, and security scan pass. A clean temporary checkout of immutable v2026.9.4 installed and built successfully, executed the actual extracted tag-push step, generated the dated 2026.9.4 heading, and changed no product path besides CHANGELOG.md (the managed-extension timestamp is transient and explicitly ignored by the guard)."
  "2026-09-06T19:00:26.041Z","harness:codex","Live release evidence 2026-09-06: CI run 34052956995 at immutable release commit bbc1cc553 failed only the static changelog check; all coverage shards, combined coverage, Windows/runtime, compatibility and smoke jobs passed. Canonical generation against this tag changes exactly one line, from ## 2026.9.6 to ## 2026.9.6 - 2026-09-06. The prior exact-tag Release workflow fix is shipped and still works; this continuation fixes the missing date in pre-tag preparation so main CI will not need recovery. Reuse this canonical date-stabilization lineage rather than create a duplicate. The immutable v2026.9.6 tag and active publisher remain unchanged."
  "2026-09-06T19:03:59.960Z","harness:codex","TDD evidence: the release-pipeline regression fails before the fix because the committed generated heading lacks its calendar date, then all 149 focused release/provenance/workflow tests pass with --date-from-version. A separate isolated Git fixture using the published pm-changelog 2026.9.6 package confirms the actual behavior: pre-tag output without the fallback differs from post-tag canonical output, while pre-tag output with --date-from-version is byte-identical after creating the matching tag. Fixture input and Git history are synthetic; no real tracker data is used. No threshold or changelog authority changed."
  "2026-09-06T19:04:12.119Z","harness:codex","Correction to the preceding test-count transcription: the focused run passed 183 tests across three files (34 release-pipeline, 125 hosted-analysis, and 24 release-automation contracts), not 149."
  "2026-09-06T19:13:51.793Z","harness:codex","Full coverage passed 8,506 tests across 628 files and the focused plans passed. The inherited static linked test used schema-only PM isolation and therefore failed the defect-evidence inventory against an empty tracker (zero governed terminal defects); this was a test-context mismatch, not a source or threshold failure. Set that linked plan to tracker context so it reads an isolated copy of the canonical tracker, then rerun it with unchanged gates."
  "2026-09-06T19:22:31.310Z","harness:codex","Final local verification: all 8,506 tests across 628 files passed under full coverage; the three focused release suites passed 183 tests; static quality passed with the repository tracker cloned into isolated PM context (476929 ms). The original schema-only static link was replaced with its explicit tracker-context form; the failed empty-inventory run remains recorded. The real published-generator fixture proves byte-identical pre-tag and post-tag output. Publication itself is complete: Auto Release 34051942462 and Release 34052957106 succeeded, npm latest and GitHub Release are 2026.9.6, independent published MCP/CLI verification and both clean installed-agent sessions pass. This preparation correction applies to subsequent releases; the existing tag remains immutable."
  "2026-09-06T19:37:31.708Z","harness:codex","Review correction: the prior tag-source guard shipped in 2026.9.5 and remains valid. Reusing this item for the distinct pre-tag argument defect changed its title and close time, incorrectly removing its historical changelog entry. Restore the original scope and resolution, explicitly bind release 2026.9.5, and track new preparation work under pm-071wg4 (discovered_from this item). All prior evidence and immutable history remain intact; no dates or history records are rewritten."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-04T13:39:58.430Z","harness:codex","A tag-push workflow cannot validate changelog content produced before the tag existed when the changelog generator derives release metadata from tags. Branch-vs-tag source mode is the stable contract: exact-tag sources regenerate under a mutation allowlist, while reviewed-main sources fail closed on drift."
